# Deploying

The app is a static site. Any static host works as long as unknown paths fall back to `index.html`.

## Vercel

```bash
npm install -g vercel
vercel deploy --prod
```

`vercel.json` already contains the rewrite rule.

## GitHub Pages

Pages does not support path rewrites. Either use hash routing or copy `index.html` to `404.html` after the build so deep links work:

```bash
npm run build
cp dist/index.html dist/404.html
```

## Netlify / Cloudflare Pages

Set the build command to `npm run build`, the output directory to `dist`, and add a catch-all redirect `/* /index.html 200`.

## Checklist before pointing users at it

- [ ] Contract addresses entered for the network you are using
- [ ] A dedicated RPC URL (the default public endpoints are rate limited)
- [ ] Logo at `public/logo.png`
